contrib/vhost-user-gpu: fences leave commands waiting for a reply

GET_DISPLAY_INFO and GET_EDID wait in the fence queue for the frontend's reply
(state PENDING), and their callbacks take the queue's last command for it. A
fence retiring meanwhile answered and freed every queued command with a lower
fence ID, the waiting one too (its fence ID is 0): the reply then found the
queue empty and vhost-user-gpu crashed (SIGSEGV in get_display_info_cb), or
found another command. The guest asks for the display info when the displays
change, e.g. when the SPICE client disconnects, which with rendering in flight
crashed the GPU. Fences now leave pending commands alone.

--- a/contrib/vhost-user-gpu/virgl.c
+++ b/contrib/vhost-user-gpu/virgl.c
@@ -845,6 +845,7 @@
          * so we should check all fenced cmds not just the first one.
          */
         if (cmd->cmd_hdr.flags & VIRTIO_GPU_FLAG_INFO_RING_IDX ||
+            cmd->state == VG_CMD_STATE_PENDING ||
             cmd->cmd_hdr.fence_id > fence) {
             continue;
         }
@@ -865,6 +866,7 @@
 
     QTAILQ_FOREACH_SAFE(cmd, &g->fenceq, next, tmp) {
         if (!(cmd->cmd_hdr.flags & VIRTIO_GPU_FLAG_INFO_RING_IDX) ||
+            cmd->state == VG_CMD_STATE_PENDING ||
             cmd->cmd_hdr.ctx_id != ctx_id ||
             cmd->cmd_hdr.ring_idx != ring_idx ||
             cmd->cmd_hdr.fence_id > fence_id) {
